Kernel patches for FreeBSD 15.1.  They apply with "git apply" to
releng/15.1 at 893c7c99b ("Add UPDATING entries and bump version"), in
this order:

01-mmc-sdio-function-driver.diff
	Adds SDIO support to the mmc stack, which bwfm_sdio needs: SDIO
	card discovery in mmc.c, the sdio_func layer (sdio_func.c/.h,
	sdioreg.h) and the SDIO card interrupt.  In bcm2835_sdhci.c it
	adds the card interrupt and a lock that shares the Raspberry
	Pi 4's controller fairly between the WiFi and the SD card, so
	heavy WiFi traffic can't starve the root filesystem.

02-net80211.diff
	Adds key slots 4 and 5 for the 802.11w group management key, and
	an Extended Capabilities element in management frames so newer
	access points don't treat the station as an old one.  Needed for
	802.11w and WPA3 on any bus.
